   "source": [
    "8.  What are logical operators in Python?\n",
    "   ->\n",
    "     Logical operators in Python are used to combine or modify conditional statements, resulting in a Boolean value of True or False. There are three main logical operators in Python: and, or, and not. \n",
    "-> and: Returns True if both operands are True, otherwise it returns False.\n",
    "-> or: Returns True if at least one of the operands is True, and False only if both are False.\n",
    "-> not: Returns the opposite Boolean value of the operand. If the operand is True, it returns False, and vice versa."
   ]
  },
